From fef23dd34471524afa33c2b4d71170533ec709e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 14:35:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Port the five fixes from the development repository

These were written against deepinact6102-netizen/-, which does not deploy
anywhere. Every file they touch here was byte-identical to that
repository's pre-fix state, so the changes transfer without conflict.

- The access gate opened the app unconditionally whenever the verify call
  threw, so going offline bypassed it. Replace that with a 7-day offline
  grace period measured from the last server-confirmed check, which
  cannot renew itself while offline. A non-ok response now counts as a
  communication failure rather than a rejection, so a server error no
  longer deletes a paying customer's stored code.
- The demo shared localStorage keys with the paid app on the same origin,
  so trying the demo overwrote a real shop's ordering data. Route demo
  reads and writes through a demo_ prefix, and let print.html select the
  prefix from ?demo=1.
- The tally-sheet reader dropped unparseable lines and then assigned the
  remaining numbers to items in order, so one missed line shifted every
  item after it and the shop ordered against another item's count. Match
  each item by its printed name instead; an item whose name is not found
  is left blank.
- The webhook only reacted to outright cancellation, so a subscriber
  whose card stopped working kept access for the weeks Stripe spends
  retrying. Drive access from customer.subscription.updated, keeping
  past_due deliberately valid, and notify on invoice.payment_failed
  without revoking.
- The gate was a dead end without a code, so link out to the demo and the
  purchase page.

index.html is left alone: it is the landing page here, not the redirect
the development repository has.

